course: dictionary
lesson: 1782
title: Holding on tight: the word cling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cling means to hold on very tightly, or to stick closely to something. «The frightened child clung to her mum's hand in the busy market.» The child is holding on tight, so clung is the past tense of cling.
explain: Cling can also mean to stick. «Wet clothes cling to your body» means they stick close to your skin. A gecko can cling to glass because its tiny toe hairs stick to the surface.
explain: You can also cling to an idea or a hope. If you keep believing something even when it is hard, you are clinging to it. Ask yourself: what is being held on to? A hand, a rock, a surface, or a belief?
fact: Cling means to hold on tightly, or to stick closely to something.
fact: Cling is a verb with the forms cling, clings, clung and clinging.
fact: «Clung» is the past tense: «The survivor clung to a log in the sea.»
fact: To cling to a hope or idea means to keep believing it even when it is hard.
fact: Cling film is a thin plastic sheet that sticks to a bowl or plate to cover food.
exercise: «The frightened child clung to her mum's hand in the busy market.» What did the child do? | Let go and ran away | *Held on very tightly | Laughed loudly | Sat down to rest
exercise: Ella says wet clothes cling to your body. What does cling mean here? | Float away in the wind | Come off easily | Dry out quickly | *Stick closely to something
exercise: «The survivor clung to a log in the sea.» Find and copy the past tense of cling. | survivor | log | sea | *clung
test: «A gecko can cling to glass because its toes stick to the surface.» What does cling mean here? | *Stick closely to something | Break into pieces | Fall off quickly | Shine brightly
test: «Yesterday, Sam ___ to the rope tightly.» Which word fits the gap? | cling | clings | *clung | clinging
exam: Asha says, «I still cling to the hope that the lost dog will come home.» What does cling to the hope mean? | Forget about it completely | Hold the dog's lead | *Keep believing it even when it is hard | Throw the hope away
